Hermes' default command; bare `hermes` and `hermes chat` are
equivalent. `start` is a bounded convenience alias mapped onto
upstream `chat` by main.bpp. The agent loop runs only in the
installed upstream, so ycode exits unsupported (4) here.


Examples:
hermes chat -q "Explain this repo"
hermes start --oneshot -q "one and done"


Usage:
  hermes chat [PROMPT]

Flags:
      --oneshot        With -q: answer the query and exit instead of an interactive session
  -q, --query string   Single query to seed or answer the session

Global Flags:
  -f, --file string        Strict harness configuration (default "agent.yaml")
  -h, --help               Show command help
  -m, --model string       Model override for this invocation (e.g. anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6)
      --provider string    Provider override for this invocation (e.g. openrouter, anthropic)
      --reasoning string   Reasoning effort: none, minimal, low, medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra
  -r, --resume string      Resume a previous session by id or title, or 'latest'
      --tui                Launch the modern TUI instead of the classic REPL
      --yolo               Bypass dangerous-command approval prompts


